@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+---
+id: dl-001-use-deterministic-list-local-task-identifiers
+type: decision-log
+title: "Use deterministic list-local task identifiers"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Tasks are currently stored and addressed by title, so an application cannot retain a reference that
+survives a rename. The domain may not use a clock or randomness. Existing callers must remain able to
+address a task by title.
+
+## Decision
+
+Each task list will allocate a deterministic, monotonically increasing string identifier when adding a
+task. A lookup argument will match an identifier first, then fall back to the existing title lookup.
+The identifier is preserved by all task transformations.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Identifiers are unique within a task list and stable for that list's lifetime, while remaining
+predictable in tests and compliant with the domain determinism rule. A task title equal to an existing
+identifier resolves to that identifier's task; this makes stable IDs unambiguous.
